* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* ok = !WRITEJSONROW(c, f)
*
* Writes the collection C as one line of compact JSON (JBUILD() writes a line feed inside a string as \n, so it is one line) to the
* sequential file F with WRITESEQ.  Gives 1 if it was written; 0 if C is not an object or an array (STATUS() 1020, nothing written),
* has no JSON form (STATUS() 1019, nothing written) or the write failed.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function writejsonrow(c, f)
$catalog !writejsonrow

   if jtype(c) # 'collection' and jtype(c) # 'array' then
      * not a data collection: JBUILD would stop the program.  Parsing a null string sets STATUS() 1020 (not JSON), which is what ELSE shows.
      x = jparse('')
      return 0
   end
   line = jbuild(c)
   if status() then return 0
   writeseq line to f then return 1 else return 0
end

* END-CODE
